# Financial safety

## Server authority

Never trust the client for: price, variant price, tax, shipping, coupon, inventory, payment status, order state, refund state. Recompute/validate on the backend using existing engines.

## High-risk surfaces

Inspect services + tests before changing:

- Payment (PhonePe/COD), order create/status, refunds, wallet
- Coupons / pricing engine, GST / tax, shipping charges
- Inventory decrement/restore, commission / payout

Preserve invariants from `docs/AAURIKAA_SECURITY_BASELINE_AUDIT.md` (e.g. no client variant price trust, no unpaid coupon burn, stock lifecycle).

## HOLD — do not invent

- Refund destination, method, timelines, jewellery return windows
- Client Refund Policy content
- Business credentials, GSTIN, addresses, catalogue seed data

If the SRS/audit marks **HOLD**, leave it HOLD. Mark work **BLOCKED/HOLD** — do not ship a fake policy.

## Discipline

- Prefer minimal, tested changes over redesigns
- Run affected backend tests for any financial/commerce touch
- Do not “fix” security by weakening checks
